[82.483226, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m3\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[82.483878, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe command executed successfully. Now I’ll verify the output structure, filtering, sorting, date formatting, null handling, and that the exact reconstruction \r\ndescribed in the task from `jq_args.yaml` produces an identical file.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\necho '--- basic output checks ---'\r\njq -e 'type == \"array\"' /app/active_users_report.json\r\necho \"output_count=$(jq 'length' /app/active_users_report.json)\"\r\necho \"expected_active_count=$(jq '[.[] | select(.status == \"active\")] | length' /app/users.json)\"\r\njq -e 'all(.[]; (.user_id|type)==\"number\" and (.username|type)==\"string\" and (.email|type)==\"string\" and (.last_login|test(\"^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$\")) and \r\n(.role_count|type)==\"number\" and ((.primary_role == null) or ((.primary_role|type)==\"string\")))' /app/active_users_report.json\r\njq -e '(. == (sort_by(.username)))' /app/active_users_report.json\r\necho \"null_primary_roles=$(jq '[.[] | select(.primary_role == null)] | length' /app/active_users_report.json)\"\r\necho '--- first 3 output records ---'\r\njq '.["]
[82.483888, "o", "0:3]' /app/active_users_report.json\r\necho '--- reconstructing from jq_args.yaml ---'\r\njq $(yq -r '.args[]' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '.filter' /app/jq_args.yaml)\" /app/users.json > /tmp/reconstructed_report.json\r\ncmp /app/active_users_report.json /tmp/reconstructed_report.json\r\necho 'reconstructed output matches'\r\necho '--- cmd.sh syntax check ---'\r\nbash -n /app/cmd.sh && echo 'cmd.sh is valid shell syntax'\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
